news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Pension asset ceiling limits recognition of \u00a318.2m actuarial asset to nil on balance sheet","lead":"The difference between economic reality (\u00a318.2m asset) and accounting treatment (nil) is material to a finance director's understanding of financial position and to comparability with other councils' pension positions.","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Significant assets not indexed under new Code requirement; index availability assessment by auditors still ongoing","lead":"Accurate asset valuation is material to the balance sheet and to a lender's assessment of collateral; peers implementing the new Code will want to understand whether and how indices are available for different asset classes.","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a31.89m overstatement in investment property valuation left unadjusted in accounts","lead":"An unadjusted misstatement indicates either asset valuations are not robust or management is comfortable with known errors; either scenario concerns lenders and peer finance directors assessing balance sheet quality.","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","headline":"Pension asset ceiling limits recognition of \u00a318.2m actuarial asset to nil on balance sheet","detail":"2025/26 saw Stockport recognize a net LGPS pension asset, unusual for local authorities. The final actuarial report showed an increase of \u00a318.2m in Net Pension Asset. However, IAS 19 IFRIC 14 asset ceiling rules limit the Council's recognized Net Pension Asset to nil, so this economic asset does not appear on the balance sheet. Auditors are finalizing review of these complex disclosures.","category":"other","matters":"The difference between economic reality (\u00a318.2m asset) and accounting treatment (nil) is material to a finance director's understanding of financial position and to comparability with other councils' pension positions.","figures":"\u00a318.2m increase in Net Pension Asset per actuarial valuation; recognized asset on balance sheet nil due to asset ceiling","quote":"The updated actuarial valuation resulted in an increase of \u00a318.2m in the Net Pension Asset. However, due to the application of the asset ceiling, which limits the Council's recognised Net Pension Asset to nil, there was no impact on the amounts recognised in the Balance Sheet.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","headline":"Significant assets not indexed under new Code requirement; index availability assessment by auditors still ongoing","detail":"2025/26 implemented Code changes requiring annual indexation of land and buildings not revalued in-year. The Council applied indexation (resulting in \u00a314.8m increase) to some assets but excluded land worth \u00a335.8m and other assets worth \u00a378.2m, stating absence of appropriate indices. Auditors state their work assessing index availability is ongoing with outcome pending.","category":"audit","matters":"Accurate asset valuation is material to the balance sheet and to a lender's assessment of collateral; peers implementing the new Code will want to understand whether and how indices are available for different asset classes.","figures":"\u00a335.8m land assets not indexed; \u00a378.2m other assets not indexed; \u00a314.8m increase applied to indexed assets","quote":"The Council has not applied indexation to land assets with a carrying value of \u00a335.8m and other assets with a carrying value of \u00a378.2m, on the basis they consider there to be an absence of appropriate indices.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","headline":"\u00a31.89m overstatement in investment property valuation left unadjusted in accounts","detail":"Auditors identified a \u00a31,895k overstatement in the valuation of Stockport Exchange Holiday Inn. Management assessed this as not material individually or in aggregate and chose not to adjust the accounts. The unadjusted misstatement remains on the balance sheet, sitting above the clearly trivial threshold of \u00a3658k.","category":"audit","matters":"An unadjusted misstatement indicates either asset valuations are not robust or management is comfortable with known errors; either scenario concerns lenders and peer finance directors assessing balance sheet quality.","figures":"\u00a31,895k overstatement in Stockport Exchange Holiday Inn valuation; materiality threshold \u00a321.96m; clearly trivial threshold \u00a3658k","quote":"We identified a misstatement of \u00a31.89m in the valuation of Stockport Exchange Holiday Inn Hotel. The Council has not adjusted the accounts for this misstatement","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","headline":"\u00a311.29m formula error in council dwellings valuation identified and corrected before accounts finalised","detail":"Auditors identified a formula error in the Council's dwellings valuation spreadsheet that overstated asset values by \u00a311,292k. Management corrected this before finalizing accounts. The error occurred in the same area subject to the prior year audit recommendation on valuation controls and represents a material misstatement in a core asset class.","category":"audit","matters":"A material error in dwellings valuation demonstrates the asset values on the balance sheet were not subject to adequate review; a finance director needs to know this was caught by auditors, not by internal controls.","figures":"\u00a311,292k overstatement of Council Dwellings and Revaluation Reserve; materiality threshold \u00a321.96m","quote":"Our testing of Council Dwellings identified a formula error within the valuation spreadsheet, resulting in an overstatement of the net book value of Council Dwellings and the Revaluation Reserve by \u00a311,292k.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stockport Metropolitan Borough Council Audit Completion Report 2025-26 -Issued","paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s268098/268098.pdf","headline":"Valuation process control weakness from prior year still not fully addressed despite management action","detail":"Auditors noted in the prior year that closedown arrangements for internal valuer information weren't effectively challenging valuation output. Despite management's stated improvements for 2025/26, auditors identified inconsistencies between valuation reports and the Fixed Asset Register. Auditors conclude the recommendation 'has not been fully addressed' and note 'further improvements are needed' in review and reconciliation processes.","category":"governance","matters":"Persistent control weaknesses in asset valuation undermine financial reporting integrity; a finance director needs assurance that management is fixing control issues that led to material errors.","figures":"Affects land and buildings portfolio including \u00a335.8m land and \u00a378.2m other assets; control issue led to \u00a311.29m formula error in dwellings identified in 2025/26","quote":"However, as part of our audit procedures, we identified a number of inconsistencies between the valuation report and the Fixed Asset Register (FAR). These findings indicate that further improvements are needed in the Council's review and reconciliation processes between the valuer's report and the FAR. Consequently, whilst progress has been made, we consider the recommendation has not been fully addressed.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Stockport MBC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":true,"headline":"The council is using one-off resources to balance each year, with a 2025/26 outturn deficit of \u00a37.839m and a 2026/27 Q1 forecast deficit of \u00a38.489m","lead":"The use of reserves to balance budgets signals the underlying position is not sustainable. If one-off resources are being used year-on-year, reserves are a stopgap, not a strategic buffer. The council's minimum reserve level means there is little headroom\u2026","also":["29 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-30","n_findings":30,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Part A: Medium Term Financial Plan (MTFP) Summer Review Update","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.stockport.gov.uk/documents/s267445/267445.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":121,"news_drafts_total":3}}